sequenceDiagram
  actor OPERATOR as Maintainer or operator
  participant EVAL as Failed evaluation or live observation
  participant ISSUE as Owning-repository source Issue
  participant PROJECT as Portfolio Project
  participant STEWARD as Reviewed decision by context steward
  participant PR as Reviewed change and pull request
  participant RELEASE as Pinned release and rollout
  participant POST as Post-change evaluation

  EVAL->>OPERATOR: report failure, regression, uncertainty, or observed gap with evidence
  OPERATOR->>ISSUE: open or update one typed owner Issue with bounded scope
  ISSUE-->>PROJECT: link for human triage and portfolio sequencing
  PROJECT-->>STEWARD: present planning context; no execution authorization
  STEWARD->>ISSUE: review policy, trust boundary, owner, dependency, and acceptance criteria
  OPERATOR->>ISSUE: authorize the selected bounded work through the source Issue
  ISSUE->>PR: Actions and Codex produce a tested, provenance-pinned change
  PR->>STEWARD: request independent semantic and architecture review
  STEWARD->>PR: approve, request changes, or reject; keep findings distinct from gate results
  OPERATOR->>RELEASE: decide merge, release, and any activation separately
  RELEASE->>POST: publish exact pins and record rollout evidence
  POST->>EVAL: evaluate with the same case, unit, and observation-window definitions
  EVAL->>ISSUE: route any new finding to a human-prioritized owner Issue
  Note over PROJECT,ISSUE: A result cannot create, prioritize, authorize, or recursively execute its own follow-up
